id: pm-vcs-vmmx
title: Stream arbitrary large files through fragment and range storage
description: "Replace whole-blob memory assumptions on the content path with fixed-size, content-addressed fragments: a versioned manifest object, streaming write and read that never hold more than one fragment, and byte-range access that touches only the fragments overlapping the range. Content-defined chunking, resumable transfer and benchmark-justified thresholds were part of the original statement and are NOT delivered here; they are tracked separately so this record describes what exists."
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-08-01T19:32:33.387Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-08T20:33:42.551Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-08T16:04:32.995Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-08T16:04:32.995Z"
claim_principal: pi-agent
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 2400
acceptance_criteria: "A file is written and read without ever holding more than one fragment in memory, proven by sampling while the operation is in flight rather than by a before/after delta; a byte range read touches only the fragments overlapping it; identical content stores its fragments once, asserted against the object files on disk; a stored fragment whose length disagrees with its manifest entry is refused by every read path; manifest bytes are canonical, with the total header pinned to its position and the terminating newline required"
parent: pm-vcs-b7cb
risk: high
